{"question_id": "qst_0424", "answer": "Based on Document 2 (the updated design guide), the current token-based prompt length bucket cutoffs are:\n\n- **short**: `<128` tokens\n- **medium**: `128\u20131024` tokens\n- **long**: `>1024` tokens\n\nNote: This updates an earlier char-based bucketing scheme (from Document 1: short <64, medium 64-512, long >512), which was revised due to inconsistent cohorting across tokenizers and languages.", "document_ids": ["dsid_f039509796f842cd84ba3bfb895c7132", "dsid_7f2a6f2d2de34f94a5b6f3d5d0d1f6a2", "dsid_7ac4915792d84235a2417a62190fea66", "dsid_2b0e85b89e5c46e98a1f530d4938e8a5", "dsid_5b30655bfbad465c88fedc262f1ba41e", "dsid_743654b07c204906bf497e2c35886051", "dsid_f5771de2f9414660aa0a4601ac89635e", "dsid_65a7c7e207654aed94aa1becf2f700fb", "dsid_e3b1fc10711c4837bd710b4e9cd6d142", "dsid_e5eafb9c853e415f88569e9e5a14a085"]}
{"question_id": "qst_0425", "answer": "In v1, signing/integrity is represented via the `integrity` field (a compact string), not an embedded `signature` blob. The `integrity` field is optional and supports one of three values:\n- `none`\n- `sha256-only` (checksums required; no signature)\n- `sigstore-oidc` (signature envelope stored separately; manifest contains only a reference)\n\nAlongside this, an optional `integrity_ref` field provides a URI pointing to the signature/envelope material when `integrity` is not `none`. This is an explicit update from an earlier draft where `signature` was a directly embedded blob \u2014 in v1, embedding large signature envelopes inline is avoided (e.g., to keep manifests attachable to support tickets/GitHub issues), so the actual signature/envelope is referenced externally via `integrity_ref` rather than included in the manifest itself.", "document_ids": ["dsid_2f9c99fc8ec74495b4b08c49a6083ba8", "dsid_4bc0e470f09d4e9285de8105c893bf07", "dsid_9cc3f70be4364e2795fe5251f8b5142a", "dsid_96ccda22c0374b34aaff4c2f5c7d1852", "dsid_834de01417d04878b4257f0f03ccbb88", "dsid_6e6c68e0f48244ae8fb0f0a91bcbe1ca", "dsid_232691356bfb48f2812b9f309ca2256c", "dsid_3aaf3b34598747809ecfd9177a7f4dc8", "dsid_7ae63f8612094ad1aacb857e4e5bae7f", "dsid_d7ad2c071d694ca49323fea5ce88c831"]}
{"question_id": "qst_0426", "answer": "Based on Document 1 (PRD: Cohort-driven evaluation harness, graduated A/B gates, and staged failover for Optimize f-serve), the automated rollback triggers are:\n\n- **Safety sentinel**: Immediate throttle if any safety sentinel shows **>0.3% absolute regression sustained for 5 minutes**.\n- **Composite quality**: Automatic cohort-level divert to previous stable variant if composite quality score drops **>3% sustained for 10 minutes** in that cohort.\n- **Business KPI**: Full rollback if business KPI regression **>4% sustained for 10 minutes** (updated from 5% for 5 minutes to reduce false negatives while avoiding brief KPI noise).", "document_ids": ["dsid_553e1651575a416dae6b92d019d2f9f4", "dsid_d9983194a5e84d14833c19477339b220", "dsid_63d32d910485469194533279fe28780f", "dsid_e04b32362f084d388f54be4fdd18e35b", "dsid_a1eec46d06554bbb9d47a75007ef8521", "dsid_87ca51a14670481ca02327b5fc8b6ea5", "dsid_f2ae5646c3b745e08bc89c5cda29d308", "dsid_7bde53c18ca54b0bb30483e769c6a7c1", "dsid_4184a153b18c4aa294788a3a1d3b954d", "dsid_bcc0d4b2368a4fee840b0191131a6abc"]}
{"question_id": "qst_0427", "answer": "The final po_fingerprint format is a SHA-256 hex digest (lowercase, no whitespace) of the concatenated string `PO_NUMBER|PO_LINE_UUID` (SHA-1 must not be used, and the raw string must not be sent unhashed).\n\nThe weekly invoice delivery SLA is **Tuesdays by 07:00 PT**.", "document_ids": ["dsid_d93aed75845e4a0b8126a80d8a7a5a41", "dsid_86f033ed92b84f3a8b381d09b0b95357", "dsid_da3615a733c94755ad9f72e0ea3c6f43", "dsid_bd29e7c58f0d4dcc9e666a420d0482fc", "dsid_cc4b7aaa6ade45cf892cdccdd41f5904", "dsid_a57efbf94fa14d0583fc35220169ca49", "dsid_cfad89f4f9964a43a4bcce338738586e", "dsid_6f1903fb3f814f01853907cdeb5574c7", "dsid_52197d13b9c2452a876d17b94b47ea4b", "dsid_60b2049485f4457eb04d045df4cfa088"]}
