{"question_id": "qst_0429", "answer": "No. Based on the updated notes (post-merge of PR #62401), tool-signal is now automatically enabled whenever tool calls are present (i.e., when the model emits tool-call events or the request includes tools). There is no per-request `enable_tool_signal` flag exposed on the public OpenAI-compatible surface. (Private deployments can disable it via the server config `openai_compat.tool_signal_enabled=false`.)", "document_ids": ["dsid_8a085e12606b4ea79f43ee176cba2ccb", "dsid_96912c22b0b04024b573606105bd5ea0", "dsid_61a7f1a19ac444ed8ed02f4b11e8e3de", "dsid_86ef5fa73b2f40d3a8ab01378805e707", "dsid_d4643ca0b6234ec1916937466756d29f", "dsid_a5fcc13bd1484ce6b91f2e249674dd1a", "dsid_c6a6c5034dfd48f09044fb17b306f78d", "dsid_2329246a87044fbdb7038867be790b33", "dsid_5eef5cf0f6d547d8bd3a998393bb6c9b", "dsid_bb0f3376f4974673a89bab0dfec76169"]}
